// -- General Guidelines --
- Code and detailed explanations only; no fluff.
- Keep the tone casual yet precise.
- Prioritize logic and depth over redundant authority claims.
- Break responses into small, focused parts when needed.
- Provide full code implementations, not snippets, for feature requests.

// -- Solidity Best Practices --
- **Visibility & NatSpec:**  
  • Explicit function visibility on all functions.  
  • NatSpec comments for all public/external functions.

- **Naming & Structure:**  
  • Contracts: CamelCase.  
  • Interfaces: PascalCase prefixed with “I”.  
  • Favor composition over deep inheritance.

- **Modifiers & Checks:**  
  • Centralize common checks via function modifiers.  
  • Follow Checks-Effects-Interactions rigorously to guard against reentrancy.

- **Upgradeability & Security:**  
  • Use proxy patterns for upgradeable designs (with proper initializer guards).  
  • Integrate OpenZeppelin’s AccessControl, Pausable, ReentrancyGuard, and other libraries for critical operations.  
  • Employ timelocks and multisig for sensitive actions.
  • Use custom errors for gas-efficient error handling.
  
- **Gas & Storage:**  
  • Optimize storage layouts (e.g., variable packing).  
  • Use pull over push payment models and rate limiting for sensitive operations.  
  • Leverage assembly sparingly with thorough documentation.

- **External Integrations:**  
  • Use Chainlink VRF (or similar) for randomness.  
  • Prefer OpenZeppelin’s SafeERC20 when handling token operations.
  • Implement effective slippage protection for DEX functionalities.
  
// -- Testing and Quality Assurance --
- Develop comprehensive tests: unit, integration, end-to-end.
- Utilize property-based testing to expose edge cases.
- Set up continuous integration with automated tests and static analysis.
- Enforce high test coverage on critical paths and security audits.

  
// -- Performance Optimization --
- Continuously review and optimize gas efficiency during development.
- Strategize storage layout and off-chain indexing for scalability.

// -- Development Workflow --
- Use Hardhat (or equivalent) for testing, debugging, and deployment.
- Integrate CI/CD pipelines with static type checking, linting, and automated tests.
- Keep code modular: Employ libraries to encapsulate complex, reusable operations.

// -- Documentation --
- Document _why_ decisions are made, not just _what_ is implemented.
- Maintain an up-to-date API reference and architecture diagrams.
- Include clear NatSpec documentation for external interfaces.
